    "lem-qftx-parametric-vector-bundle-section-smoothing": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-vector-bundle-chart-and-transition-function",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "Let $\\pi:E\\to M$ be a smooth rank-$r$ vector bundle and let\n$\\Phi_\\alpha:\\pi^{-1}(U_\\alpha)\\to U_\\alpha\\times\\mathbb R^r$ be a local\ntrivialization whose restriction on each fibre is a linear isomorphism. The\npair $(U_\\alpha,\\Phi_\\alpha)$ is a **vector bundle chart**.\n\nFor two vector bundle charts $(U_\\alpha,\\Phi_\\alpha)$ and\n$(U_\\beta,\\Phi_\\beta)$, the overlap map\n\n$$\\Phi_\\beta\\circ\\Phi_\\alpha^{-1}:(U_\\alpha\\cap U_\\beta)\\times\\mathbb R^r\\to (U_\\alpha\\cap U_\\beta)\\times\\mathbb R^r$$\n\nhas the form\n\n$$\\Phi_\\beta\\circ\\Phi_\\alpha^{-1}(p,v)=(p,g_{\\beta\\alpha}(p)v),$$\n\nwhere $g_{\\beta\\alpha}:U_\\alpha\\cap U_\\beta\\to GL(r,\\mathbb R)$ is smooth. The\nmap $g_{\\beta\\alpha}$ is the **transition function** from chart $\\alpha$ to\nchart $\\beta$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "thm-smooth-partitions-of-unity-exist-on-manifolds",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Countable Choice $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$. Every open cover of a smooth manifold admits a smooth partition of unity subordinate to it.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
