      "source_section": "Statement",
      "quote": "Assume ZF together with the Axiom of Choice. Let $M$ be $S^3$ or $S^4$ with its compact, connected, oriented, boundaryless smooth structure, let $N\\ge2$, and let $P\\to M$ be a smooth principal right $SU(N)$-bundle with a smooth reference connection $A_0$. Fix a basepoint $m\\in M$ and a frame of $P_m$. Equip $\\mathcal A_\\infty=A_0+\\Omega^1(M;\\operatorname{ad}P)$ with the Fréchet topology generated by suprema of all derivatives of section coefficients in a fixed finite bundle atlas. Let $\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$ consist of connections whose based holonomy action on $\\mathbb C^N$ has no nonzero proper invariant complex subspace. Let $K$ be the geometric realization of a finite simplicial complex, let $L$ be the realization of a subcomplex, and let $f:K\\to\\mathcal A_\\infty$ be continuous with $f(L)\\subseteq\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$. Then there is a continuous homotopy $H:K\\times[0,1]\\to\\mathcal A_\\infty$, fixed on $L$ and on an open neighborhood of $L$, such that $H(\\cdot,1)$ maps all of $K$ into $\\mathcal A_\\infty^*$. For every finite list of these $C^\\infty$ section seminorms $p_1,\\ldots,p_m$ and positive tolerances $\\epsilon_1,\\ldots,\\epsilon_m$, the homotopy can be chosen with $\\sup_{(s,t)\\in K\\times[0,1]}p_j(H(s,t)-f(s))<\\epsilon_j$ for every $j$.\n\n",
