      "source_section": "Definition",
      "quote": "Let $I=[0,1]$, $n\\ge1$, and $x_0\\in X$. Write $\\partial I^n$ for the points with at least one coordinate 0 or 1. The set $\\pi_n(X,x_0)$ consists of continuous $a:I^n\\to X$ with $a(\\partial I^n)=\\{x_0\\}$, modulo homotopies fixed on that entire boundary. This is a quotient by an equivalence relation by [[cor-homotopy-relative-and-path-homotopy-are-equivalence-relations]].",
