      "id": "step-3-1",
      "claim": "Choose basepoint $e_0=s(b_0)$. The maps $i$ and $r$ are based and [F2] gives $r_*i_*=(r\\circ i)_*=\\operatorname{id}_{\\pi_j(H,e)}$. But $\\pi_j(E,e_0)=0$ by [A1], so $i_*$ has zero target; the identity on $\\pi_j(H,e)$ factors through zero and is zero. Therefore $\\pi_j(H,e)=0$ for each $j\\ge1$.",
