+## Owner-requested Singer continuation — 2026-10-24
+
+This continuation supersedes the preceding historical status that the Singer carrier was absent. The item is now authored at `items/thm-qftx-singer-global-gauge-section-obstruction.md`, added to the existing A-page inventory and batch manifest, and covered by its restored proof contract. The four finite-regulator items are unchanged. The A/B pages remain YAML-frontmatter-only; A has three items and B has the two existing examples.
+
+The complete claim is unchanged: for every $N\ge2$ and every smooth principal right $SU(N)$ bundle over $S^3$ or $S^4$, in the $C^\infty$ section topologies, neither the irreducible reduced-gauge projection nor the full gauge-orbit projection has a continuous section. Irreducibility means that based holonomy on $\mathbb C^N$ has no proper nonzero invariant complex subspace; no trivial-bundle or full-holonomy restriction is imposed. The item fixes the right action $A^u=u^{-1}Au+u^{-1}du$, the constant center $Z_N$, quotient topologies, and a Sobolev intermediary with integer $k>r/2+1$.
+
+The local proof constructs a smooth reference connection from a finite trivializing cover and a subordinate partition of unity. It then applies the actual smooth principal reduced-gauge bundle and weak-contractibility suppliers, contradicts them with the dimension-specific nontrivial homotopy of the reduced gauge group, and restricts a hypothetical full-orbit section through the open saturated irreducible locus. The final restriction proves the full projection claim and the statement’s quotient-space embedding. The TikZ square only records the maps; the proof establishes the quotient and openness claims directly.
+
+Direct item dependencies, all with role `mathematical-premise`, are `def-axiom-of-choice`, `thm-smooth-partitions-of-unity-exist-on-manifolds`, `def-qftx-smooth-sobolev-gauge-configuration`, `thm-qftx-sobolev-smooth-irreducible-gauge-bundle`, `thm-qftx-irreducible-connections-weak-contractibility`, `thm-qftx-reduced-gauge-group-sphere-nontriviality`, and `lem-qftx-section-retract-obstruction`. Actual statements and proofs for the batch-56/57/58 suppliers were inspected; current `loadStep1Record`/`step1Decision` reports ready/current for the five in-run item suppliers. Published axiom-of-choice and partition-of-unity interfaces and the latter’s full local proof were inspected. The item's recomputed dependency level is 8, one above the maximum in-run supplier level 7. Batch 3 remains dependency level 3, one above its current required batches 2, 56, 57, and 58.
+
+The canonical plan section still lists the original Fubini, inverse-function, and gauge-geometry page prerequisites. `plan-spec.json` has the same original three. The current batch-3 manifest also retains the owner-authorized gauge-orbit, irreducible-connection, gauge-group-homotopy, and partitions page prerequisites needed by the restored Singer proof; these additions are bound in the cross-batch dependency array. The earlier prose-scaffold instruction to wait for a full Singer-source review is superseded by the current owner direction to author the full claim from the exact 56–58 suppliers while preserving the source limitation.
+
+Source history remains truthful. Singer's paper (DOI `https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01609471`, CMP 60 (1978), 7–12) is retained only for historical attribution. The current author did not inspect its full text; the seven historical failed access routes and three searches remain in `batch-3.coverage.json`, with no new attempt and no source-drop approval. The complete alternative proof is now recorded there with its exact dependencies. The A-page's existing source evidence remains unchanged: Skinner, §§8.1–8.1.1, PDF pp. 154–161, has the prior successful fetch stamp; Mitter–Viallet, §§I–V, printed pp. 458–472, was previously inspected in full-text web view but remains unstamped after five failed checker attempts. Neither source is used as a proof supplier for the Singer theorem.
+
+The Singer proof contract has exact supplier excerpts for [A1], [F1]–[F6], four derivations matching proof steps 1.1, 2.1, 3.1, and 4.1, and checked boundary cases including $N=2$, both sphere dimensions, every bundle sector, and the AC strength. The contract batch level is updated to 3. Cross-batch rows now use only `open`, `verified`, or `removed`; current direct 56–58 item interfaces and all seven A-page prerequisite-page edges are recorded as verified scoped checks, not independent proof approvals.
